@startuml correction-dimensions
' The N heterogeneous "dimensions" of approximate matching, each with its own
' metric/engine, unified into one joint score by a semiring. Colour groups a
' dimension with the crate that provides it.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title N-dimensional approximate matching — heterogeneous axes fused by a semiring

rectangle "**noisy channel**\nŵ = argmax ℙ(x│w)·ℙ(w)" as nc #455A64

rectangle "**DIM 1 · Orthographic**\nedit distance (a metric)\nliblevenshtein automaton" as d1 #1565C0
rectangle "**DIM 2 · Phonetic**\nZompist sound-alike\nliblevenshtein + libgrammstein" as d2 #1E88E5
rectangle "**DIM 3 · Syntactic**\nCFG membership (constraint)\nlling-llang CfgFilter" as d3 #6A1B9A
rectangle "**DIM 4 · Contextual**\n−log ℙ(w│ctx) (likelihood)\nlibgrammstein MKN n-gram" as d4 #2E7D32
rectangle "**DIM 5 · Semantic**\ncos-similarity → pseudo-ℙ\nlibgrammstein embeddings" as d5 #388E3C

rectangle "**Semiring**  (K, ⊕, ⊗, 0̄, 1̄)\n⊗ combines factors along a path\n⊕ selects among competing paths\nTropical: (min, +)   Log: (logsumexp, +)" as sr #00838F
rectangle "**joint score**\nbest correction = shortest / max-ℙ path" as js #455A64

nc --> d1 : channel
nc --> d2 : channel
nc --> d3 : prior
nc --> d4 : prior
nc --> d5 : prior

d1 --> sr
d2 --> sr
d3 --> sr
d4 --> sr
d5 --> sr
sr --> js

note bottom of sr
  The dimensions are **heterogeneous** —
  metric / likelihood / constraint. The
  semiring is the common currency that
  makes them composable. Each independent
  factor is one dimension → the WFST product
  construction makes the joint search N-D.
end note
@enduml
